invariant: INV-55
file: tls_write.c
catches: unit
reason: ch_write seals one data record under the old key before the
  answer a request owes, where RFC 9846 section 4.7.3 sends the answer
  before the next record of application data. bin/unit requires the
  KeyUpdate record first in the write after a request.

--- old
    if (t->key_update_owed) {
        return 0;
    }
--- new
    if (t->key_update_owed) {
        return 1;
    }
